<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Putins War Operation Exodus, 2022</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY text=#dcdcdc bgColor=#2b2b2b scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Putins War Operation Exodus, 2020&lt;BR&gt;The Time Is:14 June 2020, 18:00 UTC / 20:00 Bodo, Norway Time&lt;BR&gt;Nordkapp to UK&lt;BR&gt;Playable as either side&lt;BR&gt;Three (3) Days Duration&lt;BR&gt;This scenario was recommended by HalflifeExpert, thanks for the suggestion&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;After the onset of Russian military operations against Norway it was decided to move Norwegian Vessels, under maintenance or damaged, to Royal Navy ports and shipyards in the United Kingdom.&amp;nbsp; Norwegian and British yard workers worked 24/7 to get as many of the vessel’s systems up as possible, and propulsion back online. By the 14th escorts were in place and the exodus to the UK ready. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Unfortunately, HUMINT and signals intelligence tipped off the Russians and nuclear/conventional submarines were placed in intercept positions, Backfire bombers readied and a small surface action group hastily rearmed, refueled and placed underway. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;President Putin wants those convoys destroyed at all costs. NATO Likewise must shepherd the cripples to the UK at all costs.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Designer’s Notes:&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT color=red&gt;&lt;EM&gt;Unfortunately, I had to assign a track and course to the NATO vessels. The A/I couldn't plot a track for them and was stopping the vessels. Please feel free as a human NATO player to delete the track and speeds set.&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;BR&gt;1. Units with down systems had had those mounts or sensors removed. Make sure you look closely at availability of mounts and sensors for your Norwegian vessels.&lt;BR&gt;2. Only ships and submarines count for Victory Points (VPs), so aircraft down for maintenance or repair have been removed. &lt;BR&gt;3. There are two ways to gain/lose VPs, 1. sink a vessel or 2. reach the Plymouth or Portsmouth boxes. &lt;BR&gt;4. The vessels off the SW coast of Norway are tasked with sailing to Portsmouth &lt;BR&gt;5. The vessels near Bodo are tasked with sailing to Plymouth (both assignments are to spread out the shipyard duties). &lt;BR&gt;6. If a NATO vessel arrives and stays in the box for one (1) hour, NATO gains points and Russia loses points. &lt;BR&gt;7. Please do not delete the locked Portsmouth/Plymouth Box reference points (or no points!)! &lt;BR&gt;8. There are (A/I) Norwegian alert F-35s and an (A/I) Russian AAW-CAP over the Nordkapp area. The Russian AAW-CAP is to keep the F-35s from just ambushing the MPA as they round Nordkapp. These aircraft have limited loadouts for AAW only, that is deliberate, please do not add ARM/Ground munitions.&lt;BR&gt;9. Weather is good. Light middle level clouds 10-16 kft with Wind/Sea State 3. &lt;BR&gt;10. Where are the USAF/UK Royal Air Force fighters and multirole aircraft? Simple answer, engaged in the Baltics and Poland. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Originally created under CMO Version 1.01 Build 1134.1 – Data Base: DB3000 483&lt;BR&gt;An .INI and Delta File have both been provided for rebuilds&lt;BR&gt;Al “BeirutDude” Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;BR&gt;&lt;A href="mailto:Al.Sandrik@gmail.com"&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/A&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
